> Recorded outcomes and limits

The held-out next-location accuracy is 0.4375, against uniform top-1 chance 0.0625 and the motion oracle 1.0000. Its Brier score 0.2492 is worse than the uniform-probability baseline 0.0586; this short run does not produce calibrated occupancy predictions. The binary pixel confusion below uses threshold .5 across all 256 held-out pixels. It measures a different task from the source's 16-way argmax next-location accuracy.

All three validation epochs are plotted; the test pool does not select the checkpoint.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conv_lstm_history.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::ifstream input("build/recurrent-models/models/conv_lstm/history.tsv");if(!input)throw std::runtime_error("Missing source history");std::string line;std::getline(input,line);std::vector<double> epoch,loss;while(std::getline(input,line)){std::istringstream row(line);double x,y;if(!(row>>x>>y))throw std::runtime_error("Invalid history row");epoch.push_back(x);loss.push_back(y);}if(epoch.size()!=3)throw std::runtime_error("Expected all three source epochs");dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(epoch,loss,"Validation objective",{37,99,235}).points(epoch,loss,"All recorded epochs",{234,88,12},5).x_label("Epoch").y_label("Validation cross-entropy").y_ticks({1.2978,1.2984,1.2990,1.2996},{"1.2978","1.2984","1.2990","1.2996"}).title("ConvLSTM: validation history").size(950,520).save_svg("build/conv_lstm_history.svg");std::cout<<"| Epoch | Validation objective |\n|---:|---:|\n";for(std::size_t i=0;i<epoch.size();++i)std::cout<<"|"<<epoch[i]<<"|"<<loss[i]<<"|\n";}

